      "side": 1,
      "message": "just noting down what i was suggesting for the flush_work approach if that works.  protects the null set of opts-\u003edev in the spinlock before flushing work.  that would ensure that if work was pending we\u0027d exit early in the work handler. if work was busy, \n\nvoid android_device_destroy(struct android_uevent_opts *opts)\n{\n        struct device *dev \u003d opts-\u003edev;\n\tunsigned long flags;\n\t\n\tspin_lock_irqsave(\u0026opts_lock, flags);\n\topts-\u003edev \u003d NULL;\n\tspin_unlock_irqrestore(\u0026opts_lock, flags);\n\t\n\tflush_work(\u0026opts-\u003ework);\n\t\n\tif (opts-\u003edevice_id \u003e\u003d 0)\n\t\tida_free(\u0026android_ida, opts-\u003edevice_id);\n\tandroid_opts \u003d NULL;\n\tida_destroy(\u0026opts-\u003efunction_ida);\n\tdevice_destroy(dev-\u003eclass, dev-\u003edevt);\n}",
      "revId": "3d08c9a9abf7ee246936b9207d0f1130bedbbdab",
